message.reasoning_content:
The recursion occurs due to cycles. The code checks node is goalnode using `is` identity, but also should mark visited before recursing to avoid infinite loops. Currently nodesvisited set is never added. Should add node to visited before exploring successors. Also use `==`? Node objects likely compare by identity; test uses same objects. Use `node is goalnode` is fine.

Implement: in search_from, first if node is goalnode return True; then if node in visited return False; then add to visited; then iterate successors.

Also need to handle None successors? Node may have successors attribute possibly None. In test they set nodec = Node("C", None, [nodef]) etc. Node class likely defined in test. Let's inspect Node definition.{
  "command": "sed -n '1,200p' python_testcases/test_depth_first_search.py"
}

